{"ld": 1327, "paper": "HP862", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, Directing the University of Maine System to Study Student Teacher Compensation (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "h-sargent-holly", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-ankeles-daniel", "h-brennan-michael", "h-crockett-edward", "h-dodge-janice", "h-mitchell-christina", "h-murphy-kelly", "s-rafferty-joseph", "h-roeder-amy", "h-warren-sophia"], "committee_code": "EDU", "committee_name": "Education and Cultural Affairs", "summary": {"text": "This bill requires a postsecondary educational institution in the State to provide stipends to student teachers and the teachers who supervise them, referred to in the bill as cooperating teachers, in addition to mileage or travel reimbursement for student teachers. The bill also requires a school administrative unit to compensate a student teacher or cooperating teacher who serves as a substitute teacher for a partial or full school day in addition to the stipend. If a student teacher becomes employed as a teacher at a private school or at a school outside of the State upon graduation, the student teacher is responsible for reimbursing the State the total amount the student teacher received as a stipend. The bill provides that the State must provide funding to the University of Maine System for the cost of student teacher and cooperating teacher stipends.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0862&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Finally Passed", "final_disposition": {"label": "Finally Passed", "date": "2025-06-19", "governor_action": "Unsigned", "governor_action_date": "2025-06-19"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1327)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0862&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-400)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0862&item=2&snum=132",